            <ArticleTitle>Vector velocity estimation of blood flow - A new application in medical ultrasound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189-199</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1742271X17713353</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vector flow techniques in the field of ultrasound encompass different pulse emission and estimation strategies. Numerous techniques have been introduced over the years, and recently commercial implementations usable in the clinic have been made. A number of clinical papers using different vector velocity approaches have been published. This review will give an overview of the most significant in vivo results achieved with ultrasound vector flow techniques, and will outline some of the possible clinical applications for vector velocity estimation in the future.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
